Relevant columns and their potential usage
• sellers.seller_id : unique identifier for each seller; primary key when joining.  
• sellers.seller_city / sellers.seller_state : seller’s location – could be used for geographical cuts.  

• order_items.seller_id : link to sellers table.  
• order_items.order_id : link to orders / order_reviews.  
• order_items.product_id : link to products (and therefore to the translation table).  
• order_items.price : revenue generated by one item – used for total‑sales and average‑price KPIs.  
• order_items.shipping_limit_date : deadline given to the seller for handing the parcel to the carrier – proxy for packing time.  

• orders.order_id : link to order_items / order_reviews.  
• orders.order_purchase_timestamp : moment when the order was placed – starting point for packing‑time calculation.  

• order_reviews.order_id : link to orders / order_items.  
• order_reviews.review_score : 1‑to‑5 evaluation of the order – used for average review score.  

• products.product_id : link to order_items.  
• products.product_category_name : BR‑Portuguese category – bridge to the translation table.  

• product_category_name_translation.product_category_name : key to match with products.  
• product_category_name_translation.product_category_name_english : English category that we must “highlight”.  

Conditions / filters that will be applied  
1. Sellers that sold more than 100 order_items.  
2. When computing “packing time” we will use:  
   julianday(order_items.shipping_limit_date) – julianday(orders.order_purchase_timestamp).  

Below are ten exploratory → final SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progressively build the requested seller performance report.

```sql
-- 1) Sellers catalogue (id + location)
SELECT DISTINCT
       s."seller_id",
       s."seller_city",
       s."seller_state"
FROM   "sellers" AS s
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Mapping of Portuguese → English product categories
SELECT DISTINCT
       p."product_category_name",
       t."product_category_name_english"
FROM   "products"  AS p
JOIN   "product_category_name_translation" AS t
       USING ("product_category_name")
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Top‑selling sellers (raw quantity of order_items)
SELECT
       oi."seller_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "items_sold"
FROM   "order_items" AS oi
GROUP  BY oi."seller_id"
ORDER  BY "items_sold" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Link between order_items and orders (purchase moment)
SELECT DISTINCT
       oi."order_id",
       o."order_purchase_timestamp"
FROM   "order_items" AS oi
JOIN   "orders"      AS o
       USING ("order_id")
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Sample calculation of packing time (days) for each order
SELECT DISTINCT
       oi."order_id",
       ROUND(julianday(oi."shipping_limit_date")
             - julianday(o."order_purchase_timestamp"), 2) AS "packing_time_days"
FROM   "order_items" AS oi
JOIN   "orders"      AS o
       USING ("order_id")
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Average review score per seller
SELECT
       oi."seller_id",
       ROUND(AVG(r."review_score"), 2) AS "avg_review_score"
FROM   "order_items"  AS oi
JOIN   "order_reviews" AS r
       USING ("order_id")
GROUP  BY oi."seller_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Average item price per seller
SELECT
       oi."seller_id",
       ROUND(AVG(oi."price"), 2) AS "avg_item_price"
FROM   "order_items" AS oi
GROUP  BY oi."seller_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Sellers that already fulfil the “>100 items sold” condition
SELECT
       oi."seller_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "total_items_sold"
FROM   "order_items" AS oi
GROUP  BY oi."seller_id"
HAVING COUNT(*) > 100
ORDER  BY "total_items_sold" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) For each eligible seller, the English product category with the highest volume
WITH seller_over_100 AS (
    SELECT seller_id
    FROM   order_items
    GROUP  BY seller_id
    HAVING COUNT(*) > 100
),
seller_cat_rank AS (
    SELECT
        oi.seller_id,
        t.product_category_name_english,
        COUNT(*)                                     AS qty,
        RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY oi.seller_id
                     ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC)         AS rk
    FROM   order_items                    AS oi
    JOIN   products                       AS p  USING (product_id)
    JOIN   product_category_name_translation AS t
           USING (product_category_name)
    GROUP  BY oi.seller_id, t.product_category_name_english
)
SELECT
       scr."seller_id",
       scr."product_category_name_english" AS "top_category_en",
       scr."qty"
FROM   seller_cat_rank AS scr
JOIN   seller_over_100 AS so
       ON scr.seller_id = so.seller_id
WHERE  scr.rk = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL comprehensive seller performance report
WITH seller_stats AS (
    SELECT
        oi.seller_id,
        COUNT(*)                                           AS total_items_sold,
        SUM(oi.price)                                      AS total_sales,
        AVG(oi.price)                                      AS avg_item_price,
        AVG(julianday(oi.shipping_limit_date)
            - julianday(o.order_purchase_timestamp))       AS avg_packing_time_days,
        AVG(r.review_score)                                AS avg_review_score
    FROM   order_items       AS oi
    JOIN   orders            AS o  USING (order_id)
    LEFT JOIN order_reviews  AS r  USING (order_id)
    GROUP  BY oi.seller_id
    HAVING COUNT(*) > 100               -- keep only prolific sellers
),
top_cat AS (
    SELECT
        seller_id,
        product_category_name_english
    FROM (
        SELECT
            oi.seller_id,
            t.product_category_name_english,
            COUNT(*)                              AS qty,
            RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY oi.seller_id
                         ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC)  AS rk
        FROM   order_items                    AS oi
        JOIN   products                       AS p  USING (product_id)
        JOIN   product_category_name_translation AS t
               USING (product_category_name)
        GROUP  BY oi.seller_id, t.product_category_name_english
    )
    WHERE rk = 1
)
SELECT
       ss.seller_id,
       ss.total_items_sold,
       ROUND(ss.total_sales,          2) AS total_sales,
       ROUND(ss.avg_item_price,       2) AS avg_item_price,
       ROUND(ss.avg_review_score,     2) AS avg_review_score,
       ROUND(ss.avg_packing_time_days,2) AS avg_packing_time_days,
       tc.product_category_name_english  AS top_selling_category_en
FROM   seller_stats AS ss
LEFT JOIN top_cat    AS tc USING (seller_id)
ORDER BY ss.total_items_sold DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries walk from simple inspections to the final report delivering, for every seller who sold more than 100 products, total sales, average price, average review score, average packing time, and the English name of their best‑selling product category.
